The successful application will report to the Manager: Maintenance Planning
RESPONSIBILITIES:
Operations
Updating SAM and capturing daily ATLR’s flight hours and landings;
Filing and scanning hard copy paperwork;
Separate incoming paperwork daily for assigned aircraft;
Identify all discrepancies on ATLRs;
Identify missing log pages;
Identify and communicate Hour and Cycle differences between SAM and ATLR’s;
Update all part changes;
Verify certs received and file update status from Vendor;
Update work orders, ADs, SBs, EOs, STCs, Repairs, etc. Into SAM and file documents;
Forward all documents requested by other departments;
Capturing of work pack, If Required;
Must be open to work overtime to capture ATLR’s;
Adhoc records queries or requests
Compliance / Risk
Adhere to statutory regulations, organisational standards, policies and procedures;
Report non-compliance and implement corrective actions to ensure compliance.
Stakeholder Management
Analyse Stakeholder needs and identify improvement initiatives.
REQUIREMENTS:
Grade 12;
Must have experience in records systems;
Previous experience of Aircraft documentation will be advantageous;
Experience with technical maintenance system, SAM, will be advantageous;
Proficient in the use of Microsoft Office (Word, Excel and Outlook).
PERSONAL ATTRIBUTES:
Act with integrity and professionalism;
Following instructions & procedures;
Presenting and communicating information;
Adhering to principles and values;
Coping with setbacks & pressures;
Communication skills (Verbal & written);
Good administrative skills;
Good listening skills;
Must be accurate with data capturing;
Good time keeping.
